WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.660
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.660
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.560
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.500
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.360
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:02:00.630
<b>Thanks to Altargaia (reminder: this is the mushroom's name)...</b>

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.520
Hurry! We don't wanna 
be turned into zombies!

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.980
Let's take a break.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.880
Boy, what a mess.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.180
But, seriously...

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.620
Thanks a lot for saving me.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.960
Hey, no problem!

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.400
Oh, and I got this back for you.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.280
Hey, thanks!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.360
But...

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.490
I can't believe you're so weak 
you can't even bend iron bars.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.700
I think most humans can't, actually!

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.160
I think you're the one who's 
way stronger than you look—

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.000
Hey! Big Sis Carla!

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.620
F-Fugitive!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.330
Don't make it sound sordid!

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.910
Just kidding. It's a joke.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.780
That must have been some 
hard time you served.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.100
Can you please not make it 
sound like I'm an ex-con?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.450
Alvin-san!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:57.750
Carla-chan convinced the zombies 
not to turn you into one of them!

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.200
<i>You</i> did?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.320
P-Please, don't get the wrong idea...

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:07.020
I merely explained that it would 
do them more harm than good.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.920
There's no need to thank me.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.300
That must have been a very rousing speech.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.900
By the way, I've been wondering...

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.660
What is that?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.320
Oh, that?

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.680
It's a magic circle designed to bring 
back the soul of Maria-san's sister.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.950
Her sister's soul?

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:30.470
Are you saying she's... your 
sister is... you know...

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.310
It's all right to ask.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.680
My sister was very foolish.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.720
She was a girl who loved 
to invent new games.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.840
I never thought...

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.710
I never thought she'd try an astral projection 
game and end up a wandering spirit!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.630
That is an unusual story.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.020
So you've been wandering graveyards 
looking for your sister's soul?

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:05.230
Cemeteries do tend to 
attract them, after all.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.990
If her soul were in the land of the 
dead, I could call it back, but...

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:12.950
For better or for worse, 
it appears to still be wandering.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.130
And that's when the all-purpose healer 
who can also use summoning magic

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.230
enters the picture!

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.230
Too bad you're worthless as a healer!

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.070
So, are you saying you can do it?

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.350
A foolish question! As expected!

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.020
For me, it's a greasy steak!

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.460
You mean piece of cake?

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.020
Easy as delta!

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.590
You mean easy as <i>pie</i>?

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.450
But I can't do it all on my own.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.890
So please, Maria-san, take my hand.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:38.830
Your hand?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.000
Yes.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.350
Now think hard about your sister.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.730
I will infuse those thoughts 
with magic power,

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.440
and channel them into the circle.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.500
If all goes well, your sister 
will be drawn to your thoughts,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.330
and I'll be able to summon her.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.900
And then, Alvin-san...

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.940
Oh? Is there some way I can help?!

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.310
Please stand there and watch attentively!

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.610
Did I need to hear that?

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.060
Let us begin, Maria-san!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.830
Yes!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.980
It's very quiet.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.580
It's getting cloudy?

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.150
Alvin...

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.340
Look!

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.200
What?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.490
Hold it, hold it, hold it, hold it!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.480
Carla, stop! Open your eyes!

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.730
Stop!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.670
What is it? I'm trying to focus!

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.200
This is really not the time!

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.460
That thing looks freaky!

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.950
You called up a freaky thing!

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.080
What are you so upset about?

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.650
What is that?

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.100
That's what I was asking!

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.750
Maria-san!

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:20.610
Get hold of your senses!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.360
I'm afraid it was a failure!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.530
No time for the spell! 
We need to get out of here!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.630
Ellie!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.930
I finally found you!

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.750
Sister?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.890
That's your sister?!

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.080
Mwa ha ha!

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.740
I have possessed the body of 
this beautiful young girl!

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.040
B-But not for long!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.590
Holy Beam!

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.000
Ugh!

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:01.350
Erk... Oh, the pain!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.220
Uh. What in the world are you doing?

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.040
Um, now...

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.730
Release Carla-chan's body 
now, filthy specter!

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.200
Seriously, what are you doing?

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.230
Are you listening?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.080
Seriously, what the hell are you doing?!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.570
I'm sorry.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:26.170
Ellie really wanted to play this game 
while she was still a disembodied soul.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.810
This is one heck of an avant-garde game!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.020
I played the righteous healer.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:37.670
Carla-chan played the necromancer 
possessed by the evil spirit.

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.940
And Ellie was playing 
the evil spirit itself!

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.560
That casting seems pretty spot-on.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.120
Are you saying I look like an evil spirit?!

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.950
O-Of course not! 
It's just a figure of speech!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.570
Please don't kill me!

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.820
And it's odd to call me 
a necromancer, isn't it?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:53.760
Isn't it?

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.820
I think it's perfect casting, personally!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.820
<b>Perfect</b>

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.820
<b>Perfect</b>

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.230
Now, Ellie.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.780
If you're satisfied, 
won't you return to your body?

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.580
Yes!

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.830
Speaking of which, where is 
your little sister's body?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.440
Oh, I left it back there.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.090
I'll bring it now.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.670
She's been carrying her little 
sister's body all around with her?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:16.890
A body without a soul will rot if you don't cast 
anti-putrefaction spells on it from time to time!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.120
I see!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.030
Here we are!

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.650
She's carrying her!

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.060
And it's a really bad look!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.200
You've been carrying her 
around just like that?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.760
Ellie's a little girl. She's easy to carry.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.530
That's not what I meant!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.870
It's been so long!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.650
Wow. So this is Ellie-san's body?

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.120
Who's that?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.370
It's Ellie-san, of course!

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.980
Yeah, me!

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.120
They don't look anything alike!

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:52.930
The soul's appearance reflects 
a person's mental state,

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.520
so there may be a slight difference.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.420
That doesn't fit any definition 
of "slight" that I know of.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.780
Okay, I'm heading back in!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.230
Hey! Is she in pain?!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.320
Ellie!

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:25.480
Goodness! It's because she dived 
back in without stretching first!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.420
I don't think that's it!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.680
Get back, both of you!

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:29.890
Leave this to me!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.670
I'll cast a sedation spell!

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.420
Brute force!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.190
There. She seems to have calmed down.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.430
Because you put her down! With brute force!

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.760
Ellie, wake up!

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:50.860
Ellie!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:55.550
What? Am I back in my body?

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.400
Yes. You're all back to normal!

00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.860
Good grief. Well, you seem 
to be completely recovered.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.640
Big Sis Carla, you saved me!

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:06.240
Though it did hurt for 
a minute back there...

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.760
But I'm back in my body!

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.760
I guess it averaged out?

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.310
I suppose we'll be on our way.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:24.660
Thank you for everything.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.720
Thank you, Big Sis Carla!

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.510
Under normal circumstances, I couldn't 
allow a necromancer to remain at large...

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:33.730
but I suppose I'll let you go, this time.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.410
Thank you very much.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.810
But next time, I play the healer, okay?

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:41.910
Right!

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.250
Now, let's return to our village.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.290
Right!

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:01.620
Oh, right...

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.510
I should really say goodbye 
to the zombies first.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:06.930
Goodbye!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.170
Come by our village any time!

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.940
I'd love to play again sometime!

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:22.750
Looks like they're gone.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.580
It's not really worth crying over, is it?

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.480
But...

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.990
Come on. Making friends is 
a good thing, isn't it?

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:37.520
So don't cry! Cheer up!

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:40.070
Yes. That's right.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.620
I did make friends, didn't I?

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:47.730
Friends that you don't have.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.010
Fine, cry!

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:02.650
Maria-san was such a nice person.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.490
So elegant, and with such a kind smile...

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.580
Is that what they call a 
rejuvenating personality?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.970
That's right.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.150
Well, Carla?

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:18.370
Is that what they call a 
rejuvenating personality?

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.040
Why did you say it twice?!

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:21.760
I could say it more times than that!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.980
Is that what they call a 
rejuvenating personality?!

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.520
Enough! I get the point!

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.390
I completely understand 
what you're trying to say!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.340
Good grief.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:32.130
Are you saying you've had enough 
of her amateur rejuvenation,

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:37.230
and you're ready to turn to a professional?!

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:40.730
I've never seen anyone 
so lacking in telepathy.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.070
But very well.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.330
You do seem to have built 
up a lot of stress.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.150
I'll use a variety of mental care 
techniques to reset that for you.

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:52.210
Cool, huh?

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.260
I doubt it.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.220
I'm still in the process 
of <i>building up</i> stress.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:59.300
What kind of things do 
you find rejuvenating?

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.760
You could shut up, for a start!

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.100
You mean...

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:13.460
All you need is me, silently, by your side?!

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.500
How'd you manage to spin that one?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.360
Th-This is all really quite sudden...

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.210
Honestly, I can't believe you 
resorted to such a cliché!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:24.680
I didn't say it!

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:27.300
Oh, goodness gracious...

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.360
Such a proposal is...

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:32.900
Disgusting. I might vomit.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.360
I might get mad.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.860
I feel better now.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.830
I managed to hold it in.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.010
Safe!

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.620
I see. I managed to hold it in, too.

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.850
But if you consider my mere 
presence rejuvenating,

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.870
then how did you end up with so much stress?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.720
It's an unsolvable mystery.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.880
Solve it!

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:55.640
Maybe he's built up a 
tolerance through exposure.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.910
Yeah, like acquiring 
resistance to a toxin...

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.040
Wait, are you still here?

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:04.660
In other words, we've lost our spark!

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.890
In that case...

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:11.230
Hey, hey! Big Brother Alvin!

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:12.650
Kyapi!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.510
Cawwa is hunggy!

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:16.360
Kyapi!

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:19.700
Pwease buy samwiches and miwk wight away!

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.550
Kyapi!

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.580
I'm gonna punch that speech 
tic right out of you!

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.340
What, that wasn't rejuvenating?

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.740
I was was going for the 
"needy little sister" archetype.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:29.710
That's an insult to little 
sisters everywhere!

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:32.430
And your performance of 
it was absolute trash.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:36.660
And of course, you're not the right 
age to be an older brother...

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.540
Yes, but that's not the point!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.860
Good grief.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:45.170
I'll just have to bust 
out my ace in the hole.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.230
Am I still trapped in this circle of hell?

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:48.820
Fetch <i>that!</i>

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.400
Got it!

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:54.750
Wait over there while I 
get ready, Alvin-san.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.170
I'll keep playing along.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:04.820
I'm ready!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.150
Meow!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.470
What do you think? Meow!

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.740
Cats represent true rejuvenation of spirit!

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:14.940
Cat girls even more so!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:15.600
Meow!

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.030
And as healers like me are 
synonymous with rejuvenation,

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.050
combined, our effect is a hundred fold!

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:22.890
Meow!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.900
<b>Meooow</b>

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.440
Meooow!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.060
Triumph!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:33.650
And the "Meow" speech tic increases 
the healing further, meow!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:36.580
Where the world did you get that thing?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.610
In fact...

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:39.780
Don't you feel embarrassed 
to be dressed up like that?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.550
But, well, if that's how 
you're comfortable...

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.850
What in the world are you making me wear?!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.150
Damn you!

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.050
You put it on yourself!

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:05.520
What is it?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.670
Regarding you, Alvin-san...

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.330
Me?

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:11.740
Are you about to insult me?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.890
No...

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:18.130
Earlier, I proved that I was a 
rejuvenating archetype, but...

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:20.580
Actually, you're the only 
one who thinks that.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:26.000
But although you're mostly useless, I've been 
trying to think on your positive qualities...

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.630
And I've been struggling 
to think of anything.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.260
Yep, there's the insult.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:33.650
So? Have you figured out 
my positive qualities?

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:35.510
First!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:38.600
Tell me <i>my</i> positive qualities!

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.140
Why, though?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.570
And if you say "none," 
then, as punishment...

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:46.920
I will list out your negative qualities!

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.050
Twenty-four hours a day.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.990
Twenty-four hours a day?!

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:51.390
But, seriously...

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.540
The only thing you have going 
for you is your looks—

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.450
What did you just say?!

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.740
W-Well... it's true.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.610
Say it louder! Go on!

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:03.810
You're more desperate than I thought.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.770
Okay, it's your turn.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.160
Go on, say it!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.770
My positive qualities!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:14.100
What?

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:15.760
And you'd better not say "None"!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.900
Well?

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:18.620
Go on!

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.010
Are you ignoring me?

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.960
You're so desperate it's pathetic.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.030
I can't stand to watch.

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.700
Just say something!

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.850
Well, then...

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.360
I would say my answer is the same.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:35.280
What? You think my looks are—

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.500
Yes, that's something I 
really like about you.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.620
It's very considerate, 
the way you hide them from view!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.240
That's an freakin' insult!

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.250
I never get bored around you two!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.890
<b>Depressed</b>

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.520
What's the matter, Alvin-san?

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:09.430
I lost my sword.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.770
Oh, gosh...

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.160
Don't sit on me!

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.240
You weren't inviting me to have a seat?

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.950
Of course not! I'm depressed!

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:24.160
What a waste of a sit.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:26.880
And up I go.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:28.710
You little...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:32.140
Do you remember where you last had it?

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:38.220
I know I had it when we said goodbye 
to Maria-san and her sister...

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:42.100
But you do barely use that sword...

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.640
Maybe just let it go?

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.550
H-Hey!

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:46.270
I <i>do</i> use it, sometimes!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.430
A sword is like a warrior's soul!

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.190
Really?

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.980
It's kind of impressive that you 
lost something so important...

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.320
Is it your special skill?

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:59.030
Damn it! I set her up for that one!

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.240
<b>Severely Depressed</b>

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.800
Maybe I'll just buy a new one...

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.540
Don't do that!

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.670
It's a waste!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:09.740
A waste of money?

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:13.300
Or are you saying a sword is wasted on me?

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.470
Both.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:16.040
Yeah, figured!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.450
I know!

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.810
I have a great idea!

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.210
Ta-da!

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:26.970
A crystal ball?

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.150
Yes.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:31.150
It will show us where you lost the sword.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:34.890
What, you can do divination now?

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:38.430
Such a foolish question. Typical Alvin-san.

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:41.990
Foolish Question

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:41.990
Foolish Question

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.770
I've seen people do it!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.240
Foolish Answer

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.240
Foolish Answer

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.240
Don't respond with a foolish answer!

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:48.030
Just watch.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.650
O, crystal ball!

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:54.690
Reveal to me the location 
of Alvin-san's lost sword!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:09.400
Hur! Ry! Up!

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.890
Don't rush it!

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:13.190
But Alvin-san!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.850
This stupid jerk won't do what I tell it!

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:18.010
Don't call it a jerk!

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:21.210
And just because you've seen people do 
it doesn't mean you can do it yourself!

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.720
Seriously, give it up.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.080
I know!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.530
I think I'm using it wrong!

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:37.780
This is it!

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:42.680
What are you doing?!

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.140
Go!

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:45.790
I'm not gonna fetch it! 
What am I, a dog?!

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:47.820
Woof!

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:52.560
Hey, I never said you were 
all bark and no bite!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.680
Neither did I!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:57.060
Don't throw the thing away just 
because you couldn't use it!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:00.160
Th-That's not what I did! 
What a silly accusation.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.580
Do you know where the 
crystal ball came down?

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:05.860
How should I know?

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.870
Over there somewhere...

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.320
Good grief. You're just hopeless.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:12.660
A hint!

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.700
Where is the thing you lost?

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:19.950
Are you saying the crystal ball came 
down in the place I lost my sword?!

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:21.280
Precisely!

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.460
What a load of crap!

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:27.000
I'm just gonna buy a new one...

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.070
Are you sure that's what you want to do?

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.190
Yes.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:45.600
Then, help me find my crystal ball!

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:47.410
That thing was really expensive!

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.730
Then, why did you throw it?!

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.340
Big Sis! Wasn't that fun?

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.970
I'm so glad you got to 
play your game, Ellie.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:32.910
Yeah! And now I get to do the preview, too?

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:33.800
That's right.

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:36.990
But the episode title's very 
long, so be very careful!

00:23:36.990 --> 00:23:38.150
Yes, I'll do my be—

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>"This episode features even more female guest characters hot on
the heels of Maria and Ellie and by the way even though
we jumble the order now and then we mostly follow the
source material but because the Medusa and Dryad episode
would let us get a few more rare female characters on-screen
we originally had the idea to put them in episode 2 or 3 to get
people more invested except putting them in episode 2 or 3
really would be a little too extravagant and kind of mess up the
flow so we decided against it and that's a fun little behind
the scenes anecdote but anyway now it's finally time
to reveal them and that's the deal with episode 9."</b>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:40.150
Wait, is this actually the title?!
